{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":475627,"name":"Super","username":"today","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/6a8cbe/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-27T07:04:04.879Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI am using Cursor Pro, with on-demand usage off.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere is a $20 credits monthly that allows me to spend on specific model in Cursor IDE.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI tried Grok Bot today (new registered linked up using Cursor), and I am confused about whether it affects the $20 credit or not.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe $69.94 is cost from Grok Bot, and marked as “Included in Pro”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/7/1/71a7fdb0ef04d5668d3897c199d4fbe444c56c67.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/gdrS8uH58OXZSg4D4vVD9UrMtoP.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/1/71a7fdb0ef04d5668d3897c199d4fbe444c56c67_2_690x162.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"gdrS8uH58OXZSg4D4vVD9UrMtoP\" width=\"690\" height=\"162\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/1/71a7fdb0ef04d5668d3897c199d4fbe444c56c67_2_690x162.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/1/71a7fdb0ef04d5668d3897c199d4fbe444c56c67_2_1035x243.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/1/71a7fdb0ef04d5668d3897c199d4fbe444c56c67_2_1380x324.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"1B1B1B\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e2148×506 23.2 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ewhile in Grok Bot, it shows 35% (so roughly calculated, there is a weekly $200 quota on Grok Bot?)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/2/f/2fea903d43aaa7263d296e5fe695bd8e407bb94f.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/6PSZrdIFDDOPGN2Fwd603JtdH0r.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/2/f/2fea903d43aaa7263d296e5fe695bd8e407bb94f_2_690x162.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"6PSZrdIFDDOPGN2Fwd603JtdH0r\" width=\"690\" height=\"162\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/2/f/2fea903d43aaa7263d296e5fe695bd8e407bb94f_2_690x162.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/2/f/2fea903d43aaa7263d296e5fe695bd8e407bb94f_2_1035x243.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/2/f/2fea903d43aaa7263d296e5fe695bd8e407bb94f_2_1380x324.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"131314\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1498×352 14 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy question is,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWhen Grok Bot uses AI models, does the cost count into the $20 monthly credits in Pro plan?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRight now in my account, $69.94 already used, does it mean I can no longer use specific models (non Auto mode) in Cursor?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThank you.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-27T12:16:06.511Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":856,"reads":31,"readers_count":30,"score":4251.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":169658,"topic_slug":"is-grok-bot-usage-separate-from-cursor-plan","display_username":"Super","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-spend-cursor-usage-i-cant-accept-it/169796/5","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Grok Bot spend cursor usage, I can't accept it","clicks":9},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/incorrect-model-usage-billing-sub-agent-spawned-as-composer-2-5-fast-but-billed-as-grok-4-6-high/170060/6","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Incorrect Model Usage Billing: Sub-agent spawned as Composer 2.5 Fast but billed as Grok 4.6 (high)","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":134728,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/is-grok-bot-usage-separate-from-cursor-plan/169658/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":477780,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-29T19:22:14.288Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the request, the screenshots really help clear things up. Point by point:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo, Grok Bot usage does not spend your Pro credit of 20 USD per month for specific models in Cursor IDE. Grok Bot on Pro has its own separate included weekly allowance, tracked separately. The percentage meter inside Grok Bot (like the 35%) is the accurate indicator of Grok Bot usage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, the 69,94 USD shown for Grok Bot did not use any of your 20 USD for Other Models. Specific models (non Auto) in Cursor are still available as usual.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportant note about pool isolation: the separation only works within Grok Bot’s included weekly limit. Once that weekly pool is used up, any further Grok Bot usage, if you have On-Demand enabled, goes into the shared On-Demand pool, the same one used for the rest of Cursor usage. You have on-demand turned off, so spillover can’t happen right now. After the weekly pool is exhausted, Grok Bot will just hit the limit instead of charging anything. If you ever enable on-demand and want to be safe, you can set an On-Demand limit on \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e in Dashboard \u0026gt; Usage / Billing, including 0 USD to fully prevent spillover. More details: \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/help/grok-bot/plans\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003ePlans and billing | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy Grok Bot lines still show up on the Cursor dashboard as Included in Pro: both products run under one account and shared billing, so usage is shown together even though limits come from different pools. The dashboard does not currently split usage by product, and I know that can make it look confusing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if anything still doesn’t line up.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-08-29T19:22:14.288Z","